From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:34:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 501/503] Consume explicit routed input quantization

Base: vLLM 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus the immutable 188-patch r6x steering series (ebb44766d6f04d3a9272b712778d7f2fa2cec1fd).

Rationale: Expose q and scale dependencies through opaque MoE entries and reuse them only for a verified row-preserving consumer.

Quality: preserve BF16 boundaries, steering and the existing routed/shared arithmetic. Candidate disabled by default; non-SP target TP4 SM121 scope only. No adoption or performance claim.

Tests: source AST, standalone CPU host contracts and diff checks. Torch dispatcher, TileLang compilation, GPU differential/capture, model quality and capacity/performance gates remain unexecuted.

Upstream status: isolated downstream experiment in imDaniel/spark-ds41f; not submitted upstream.
